+# Conventions
+- Runtime is strict-mode CommonJS with extensionless local `require` calls used widely.
+- Neostandard/StandardJS style: 2-space indentation, no semicolons, no trailing commas; max line length 120 with configured exceptions.
+- Prefer small lifecycle-preserving changes; Fastify is performance-sensitive and commonly caches lazily behind symbols from `lib/symbols.js`.
+- Public runtime API changes must remain aligned with `types/` declarations and `docs/Reference/`.
+- Tests use `node:test`, often `const { test } = require('node:test')`, and `t.assert`.
\ No newline at end of file
